Project Objective
The objective of this project is to identify and classify harmful or toxic language in user-generated comments.
The project simulates a real-world content moderation and AI data annotation task in which annotators must distinguish between different forms of harmful communication while avoiding false positives.
The project will assess the ability to:
1.	Identify toxic language.
2.	Distinguish between different types of toxicity.
3.	Apply annotation guidelines consistently.
4.	Handle ambiguous and borderline comments.
5.	Recognize when a comment contains more than one toxic category.
6.	Separate criticism, disagreement, sarcasm, and offensive language.
7.	Perform quality assurance on completed annotations.
